      "x": 68,
      "y": 471.3748999999999,
      "width": 246.1914,
      "fontSize": 7.8,
      "font": "Helvetica"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "4. Discussion",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 88.8806,
      "width": 72.6132,
      "fontSize": 13.2,
      "font": "Times-Bold"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "In a rural cohort in which confirmatory testing is systematically delayed, gating escalation on an adaptive",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 109.7441,
      "width": 429.3689999999999,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "marker panel was associated with a shorter time-to-therapeutic intervention and lower 28-day mortality. The",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 124.14410000000001,
      "width": 441.01739999999995,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "effect size was consistent across sensitivity analyses and across sites of very different baseline volumes.",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 138.54410000000001,
      "width": 422.841,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "Several caveats bound this conclusion. Our design is observational, and gating was not randomised; sites that",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 158.9441,
      "width": 444.465,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "introduced gating may differ in ways that the recorded covariates do not capture. The mechanism by which",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 173.3441,
      "width": 436.09079999999994,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "earlier escalation is achieved is plausible but was not directly measured. And the wider registry literature on",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 187.7441,
      "width": 439.06919999999997,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "triage gating is itself uneven: the report by Mehra et al. (2020) was later withdrawn by the publisher after",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 202.1441,
      "width": 428.45099999999996,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "concerns were raised about its source data, so the extent to which our estimates inherit that lineage requires",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 216.54410000000001,
      "width": 437.22299999999996,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "separate consideration rather than assumption.",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 230.94410000000002,
      "width": 188.9448,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "Our finding is therefore best read as a hypothesis about organisational delay that warrants prospective",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 251.3441,
      "width": 414.2832,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "evaluation, not as a settled estimate of effect. A stepped-wedge trial, in which sites introduce gating in sequence,",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 265.7441,
      "width": 458.388,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "is the natural next design and would separate the intervention effect from secular trends in sepsis recognition.",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 280.1441,
      "width": 445.50539999999995,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "5. Conclusions",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 303.68059999999997,
      "width": 81.4176,
      "fontSize": 13.2,
      "font": "Times-Bold"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "Taken together, these data support routine marker-panel gating in rural emergency departments, reducing",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 324.54409999999996,
      "width": 427.41059999999993,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "time-to-therapeutic intervention by 31%. The effect was not explained by differences in case mix, and was",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 338.94409999999993,
      "width": 433.6121999999999,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "stable when the analysis was restricted to sites that contributed fewer than one thousand eligible presentations.",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 353.3440999999999,
      "width": 449.871,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "Prospective, prospectively governed evaluation is required. Until such evaluation is available, the present",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 373.74409999999995,
      "width": 427.14539999999994,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "findings should be read as evidence that the question is worth asking, and not as evidence that gating is",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 388.1440999999999,
      "width": 419.832,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "text": "effective.",
      "x": 68,
      "y": 402.5440999999999,
      "width": 37.566599999999994,
      "fontSize": 10.2,
      "font": "Times-Roman"
    },
    {
